short-code {"wall_s": 6.523495167, "ttft_s": 0.4248989590000001, "text": "Here is a complete Python LRU cache implementation with a doubly linked list, a dictionary, and comprehensive unit tests.\n\n```python\nimport unittest\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\n\n\nclass Node:\n    \"\"\"Node for doubly linked list.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, key, value):\n        self.key = key\n        self.value = value\n        self.prev = None\n        self.next = None\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    \"\"\"LRU Cache using doubly linked list and dictionary.\"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, capacity):\n        self.capacity = capacity\n        self.cache = {}  # key -> Node\n        self.head = Node(None, None)  # dummy head\n        self.tail = Node(None, None)  # dummy tail\n        self.head.next = self.tail\n        self.tail.prev = self.head\n        self.size = 0\n    \n    def _remove_node(self, node):\n        \"\"\"Remove a node from the linked list.\"\"\"\n        node.prev.next = node.next\n        node.next.prev = node.prev\n    \n    def _add_to_tail(self, node):\n        \"\"\"Add a node to the tail (most recently used).\"\"\"\n        node.prev = self.tail.prev\n        node.next = self.tail\n       ", "reasoning": "", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 58, "completion_tokens": 256, "total_tokens": 314, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 58}}, "finish": "length", "done": true, "temperature": 0, "case": "short-code", "thinking": false}
short-story {"wall_s": 6.428975708000001, "ttft_s": 0.3431104999999999, "text": "The salt spray stung Elias\u2019s face as he hauled the last crate of oil up the spiral stairs. The lamp, a monstrous brass beast, was already lit, its beam cutting a pale, trembling path across the black Atlantic. He was sixty-one, and his hands knew the rhythm of the wicks better than his own heartbeat. The storm outside was a screaming, wet fury, but inside the lighthouse, it was just the hum of the flame and the groan of the stone.\n\nHe was about to settle into his chair, a worn leather thing that smelled of pipe smoke and old coffee, when he saw it. A small, damp envelope, sealed with a blob of red wax, resting on the cold iron of the lamp\u2019s base. It hadn\u2019t been there an hour ago. He hadn\u2019t heard a knock, a footstep, or the creak of the door. He picked it up, feeling the slick, cold paper. The wax was cracked, and the seal was a strange, swirling symbol he didn\u2019t recognize.\n\nHe opened it. The paper inside was thick, almost parchment-like, and the handwriting was a tight, elegant scrawl.\n\n*Elias,*\n\n*The storm will break at 2:14 AM. The", "reasoning": "", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 57, "completion_tokens": 256, "total_tokens": 313, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 57}}, "finish": "length", "done": true, "temperature": 0, "case": "short-story", "thinking": false}
short-reasoning {"wall_s": 6.471927624999999, "ttft_s": 0.38182899999999975, "text": "To determine the number of workers needed, we follow these steps:\n\n**1. Calculate total required capacity (including the reserve):**  \n- The service receives **120 requests per second**.  \n- We must reserve **25% of total capacity** for spikes. This means the actual capacity must be **125%** of the incoming load (100% for normal traffic + 25% reserve).  \n- Required capacity = 120 requests/sec \u00d7 1.25 = **150 requests/sec**.\n\n**2. Determine capacity per worker:**  \n- Each worker handles **20 requests per second**.\n\n**3. Calculate the number of workers:**  \n- Workers needed = Required capacity \u00f7 Capacity per worker  \n- 150 \u00f7 20 = **7.5 workers**.\n\n**4. Round up to the nearest whole number:**  \n- Since we cannot have a fraction of a worker, we round up to **8 workers**.\n\n**Arithmetic check:**  \n- 8 workers \u00d7 20 requests/sec = **160 requests/sec** total capacity.  \n- Reserve capacity = 160 \u2212 120 = **40 requests/sec**, which is **33.3%** of the incoming load (40 \u00f7 120 = 0.333).  \n- This exceeds the required 25% reserve", "reasoning": "", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 71, "completion_tokens": 256, "total_tokens": 327, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 71}}, "finish": "length", "done": true, "temperature": 0, "case": "short-reasoning", "thinking": false}
